  {"file": "tests/action/insights/basic.rifts", "line": 5, "column": 16, "endLine": 5, "endColumn": 17, "category": "stack", "kind": "frame", "placement": "above", "message": "stack frame of sum: 24 B reserved on entry, about 0 B optimized — v 24 B", "detail": "Every stack slot of a function is reserved when it is entered (one adjustment of the stack pointer), whichever scope declares it: a variable declared near the end of a block has its slot from the start, and slots are not resized as scopes open and close. Sizes are before alignment padding. Optimized builds keep only the slots whose address is used (passed by reference, indexed); the others live in registers.\n\n| slot | type | bytes | what | optimized |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `v` | `big` | 24 | parameter | registers |\n"},
